description:
## what

`keyrack unlock` on an `aws.config` (sso) key cannot recover when the browser holds a portal session for a different sso user than the key's `awsSsoUsername`. it reports `✓ logged out, retry login...`, the retry reuses the same wrong browser session, and it dies with `sso login failed; session still invalid — fix: complete browser auth`.

seen on rhachet 1.51.0 (latest), aws cli v2 (pkce default), two users on one identity center start url.

## root cause

`clearAwsSsoCacheForDomain` assumes a server-side `LogoutCommand` "kills the browser session too". it does not. `LogoutCommand` revokes the cli token only; the browser's portal session survives, and the pkce `aws sso login` (default since cli 2.22) reuses it with one "allow" click, as the same wrong user. no cli call can end the browser session; only a sign-out in the browser does.

proven live (patched build, output below): the logout matched 1 cache entry, deleted it, and `LogoutCommand` succeeded, yet the retry still came back as the browser's user.

```
├─ ⚠ session invalid, logout browser session...
│  ├─ start url: https://<redacted>.awsapps.com/start
│  ├─ cache: 39 scanned, 1 matched, 1 deleted
│  └─ ✓ server session signed out
├─ ✓ logged out, retry login...
💥 sso login failed; session still invalid
```

two adjacent defects, same path:
1. `✓ logged out` prints unconditionally; a failed `LogoutCommand` is swallowed into `skipped` and never shown
2. the unlock retry (`triggerSsoLogin`) pipes all aws output, so the wait for browser approval is silent, and the human sees no authorize link (the new-login path in `setupAwsSsoProfile` already streams it)

## fix (proven with a pnpm patch)

in `confirmSsoSessionForUser`, between the logout and the retry:
- report the logout outcome: start url, cache scanned/matched/deleted, each skip reason, and `✓`/`✗` for the server sign-out
- hand the browser sign-out to the human: print `✋ the browser still holds the other user's portal session`, open the start url (`open` / `xdg-open`, best effort; the url is printed as fallback), wait for enter. no tty → no wait, print the hint
- then retry the login

also:
- `triggerSsoLogin`: inherit stdin and print the authorize link (and device code, if any) as soon as aws emits it, as `setupAwsSsoProfile` does
- start url compare in `clearAwsSsoCacheForDomain` tolerates an end `/` or `#/` fragment
- final error hint: `sign in as <user>: sign out of the aws access portal in your browser (or use a private window), then rerun`

result with the patch, browser held the wrong user:

```
├─ ⚠ session invalid, logout browser session...
│  ├─ start url: https://<redacted>.awsapps.com/start
│  ├─ cache: 39 scanned, 1 matched, 1 deleted
│  └─ ✓ server session signed out
├─ ✋ the browser still holds the other user's portal session
│  ├─ open: https://<redacted>.awsapps.com/start
│  ├─ sign out there (top right, then "sign out")
│  └─ then press enter here, and sign in as <user>
├─ retry login...
└─ ✓ authenticated as <user>
```

the authorize-link part (triggerSsoLogin) is in the patch, not yet run live.

## clamps owed upstream

- unlock where the first check is invalid and the browser holds another user: the human is prompted to sign out before the retry
- a failed `LogoutCommand` renders `✗`, never `✓`
- the retry prints the authorize link

## patch

refs: aws docs, sign out of the aws access portal (`docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/howtosignout.html`); aws cli pkce sso (`aws.amazon.com/blogs/developer/aws-cli-adds-pkce-based-authorization-for-sso/`)

the pnpm patch against 1.51.0 `dist/`, below. port to the `src/` equivalents:
- `domain.operations/keyrack/adapters/vaults/aws.config/clearAwsSsoCacheForDomain.ts`
- `domain.operations/keyrack/adapters/vaults/aws.config/vaultAdapterAwsConfig.ts` (`triggerSsoLogin`, `confirmSsoSessionForUser`, new `awaitBrowserPortalSignOut`)

